# ── gen491 (2026-09-01) — PERCHE' LE ATTESE «Learned: pred(arg)» SONO CAMBIATE ─
#
# Questo file asseriva la NOTAZIONE come risposta attesa: «Learned: man(socrates).»
# Un ratchet che congela un difetto lo difende con l'autorita' di un verde, ed
# era il caso: la risposta principale di parrot0 non era LINGUA, e l'audit
# dell'eco (scripts/self_echo_audit.py) ha mostrato che rileggendosi parrot0
# chiamava la propria notazione «a snippet of code» — non la riconosceva come
# propria.
#
# Le attese sono state ritirate, non allineate a un comportamento qualunque: la
# sostituzione e' avvenuta SOLO dove il vecchio atteso era un termine e il nuovo
# e' la frase corrispondente. L'invariante che regge il cambio sta in
# tests/p0t/conversation/self_echo.p0t — tutto cio' che parrot0 dice deve
# essergli comprensibile — e adesso la conferma e' un punto fisso:
#
#     > a whale is a mammal      →  Learned: whale is a mammal.
#     > whale is a mammal        →  Learned: whale is a mammal.
#
# migrated from tests/cases/factsource.chat (gen346, hermetic + isolated)
[mock hermetic]
!set PARROT0_BASE=
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test factsource]
# deep-reasoning M1 (docs/plans/deep-reasoning.md §4bis): PROVENANCE. Every fact the
# comprehension parser EXTRACTS keeps the raw source fragment it came from, as
# fact_source(FactRepr, Concept, "raw"). This is the prerequisite for self-correction
# (M4): the deep-reasoning loop can return to a suspect fact's source and re-check it.
# Hermetic base -> every fact is genuinely learned, and its source genuinely recorded.

# Extract a locative fact -> it is stored WITH its source fragment.
> France is located in Western Europe
< Learned: france is located in western europe.
# ...and the source is queryable by concept.
> where did you learn about France?
< I learned located_in(france, western_europe) from: "france is located in western europe".

# A membership fact carries provenance too.
> A whale is a mammal
< Learned: whale is a mammal.
> what is your source for whale?
< I learned mammal(whale) from: "a whale is a mammal".

# Honest: a concept with no recorded extraction has no source (never invented).
> where did you learn about Mars?
< I don't have a recorded source for mars.

